.TH FLOW-UI 1 "November 2026" "ETL Madness FlowUI 1.3.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
flow-ui \- ETL Madness FlowUI (Flow Builder Studio) Blazor Server web application
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B flow-ui
[\fB\-\-env-file\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-urls\fR \fIURLS\fR]
[\fB\-\-contentRoot\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-service-name\fR \fINAME\fR]
.br
.B flow-ui
\fB\-\-version\fR | \fB\-\-help\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B FlowUI
(Flow Builder Studio) is an interactive .NET 10 ASP.NET Core Blazor Server web
application for visually designing, configuring, signing, encrypting,
validating, executing, and monitoring XML ETL pipelines powered by
.B go-flow
and
.BR go-flowAPI .
.PP
FlowUI is a stateless frontend that communicates exclusively with
.B go-flowAPI
over HTTP/HTTPS (REST JSON and Server-Sent Events). It does not connect
directly to application databases.
.PP
Unix packages install isolated under
.I /opt/flow-ui
alongside
.BR systemd ,
OpenRC, SysVinit, FreeBSD
.BR rc.d ,
OpenBSD
.BR rc.d ,
and macOS
.B launchd
service definitions. Windows packages install under
.I C:\eProgram Files\eETL Madness\eFlow UI\e
with native Windows Service Control Manager (SCM) support.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-env-file " PATH"
Load \fIKEY=VALUE\fR environment settings from \fIPATH\fR before initializing
ASP.NET Core and \fBAppConfig\fR. Existing non-empty process environment
variables take precedence over values in the file. Also configurable via
\fBFLOW_UI_ENV_FILE\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-urls " URLS"
Semicolon-separated Kestrel listen URLs (e.g., \fIhttp://0.0.0.0:5185\fR).
Overrides \fBFLOW_UI_PORT\fR and \fBFLOW_UI_SCHEME\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-contentRoot " PATH"
Override the ASP.NET Core content root directory (defaults to
\fI/opt/flow-ui/app\fR when invoked via \fI/opt/flow-ui/bin/flow-ui\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-service-name " NAME"
Windows Service name used when running under Windows SCM (default:
\fBFlowUI\fR).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display usage information and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
See
.BR flow-ui.env (5)
for the complete list of supported environment variables, including
\fBFLOW_API_URL\fR, \fBASPNETCORE_URLS\fR, \fBFLOW_UI_AUTH_MODE\fR, and
Kestrel TLS certificate settings.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /opt/flow-ui/bin/flow-ui
Launcher wrapper invoking the FlowUI application with \fB\-\-contentRoot /opt/flow-ui/app\fR.
.TP
.I /opt/flow-ui/app/
Published .NET 10 Blazor Server application, \fIwwwroot/\fR static assets, and embedded guides.
.TP
.I /etc/flow-ui/flow-ui.env
Default daemon environment configuration file on Linux and OpenBSD (\fI/usr/local/etc/flow-ui/flow-ui.env\fR on FreeBSD, \fI/opt/flow-ui/etc/flow-ui.env\fR on macOS).
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/flow-ui.service
Native systemd service unit on Linux.
.TP
.I /usr/local/etc/rc.d/flow_ui
FreeBSD
.BR rc.d (8)
service script (\fI/etc/rc.d/flow_ui\fR on OpenBSD).
.TP
.I /var/lib/flow-ui
Runtime state and ASP.NET Core Data Protection key directory (\fI/var/db/flow-ui\fR on FreeBSD, OpenBSD, and macOS).
.SH EXAMPLES
Start FlowUI interactively against a local go-flowAPI instance:
.PP
.RS
.nf
FLOW_API_URL=http://localhost:8080 ASPNETCORE_URLS=http://127.0.0.1:5185 flow-ui
.fi
.RE
.PP
Enable and start the Linux systemd service:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo vi /etc/flow-ui/flow-ui.env
sudo systemctl enable --now flow-ui.service
sudo journalctl -u flow-ui.service -f
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR flow-ui.env (5),
.BR systemctl (1)
.SH AUTHOR
ETL Madness <https://github.com/etl-madness/flowUI>
